Subject: [PATCH] serial: core: retain the low-level module for live TTY objects

Set the owner before tty_register_driver() publishes the TTY driver. TTY
open and final release then hold and drop a reference to the low-level
UART module. Preserve the existing owner if no low-level one was supplied.

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
@@ -2783,3 +2783,7 @@ int uart_register_driver(struct uart_driver *drv)
+	/* Keep the low-level driver alive until the TTY is released. */
+	if (drv->owner)
+		normal->owner = drv->owner;
+
 	normal->driver_name	= drv->driver_name;
 	normal->name		= drv->dev_name;
 	normal->major		= drv->major;
